    <DataNode elementId="AT4G35830-MONOMER" textLabel="Aconitate hydratase 1" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT4G35830-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="355" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">ACO1 is an aconitase that can catalyze the conversion of |FRAME: CIT| to |FRAME: THREO-DS-ISO-CITRATE| through a |FRAME: CIS-ACONITATE| intermediate, based on the phenotype of reduced aconitase activity in an &lt;i&gt;aco1&lt;/i&gt; mutant |CITS: [17013749]|. ACO1 may participate in the TCA cycle and other primary metabolic pathways and it is believed to accumulate in the mitochondria and the cytosol |CITS: [17013749]|. Interestingly, ACO1 can specifically bind to the 5&apos; UTR of |FRAME: AT2G28190|, which encodes a superoxide dismutase, &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; and can affect the levels of |FRAME: AT2G28190| transcript accumulation &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt;. Either through this mechanism or other undiscovered mechanisms, ACO1 appears to play a role in the response to oxidative stress in Arabidopsis thaliana |CITS: [17013749]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G35830-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="Aconitase 1" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="Citrate hydro-lyase 1" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33458, RXN-33457, RXN-T9-2104, RXN-5978" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="4" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT4G35830.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT4G35830" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
